{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"youtube","name":"Ad-free YouTube","version":"0.4.3","apiVersion":1,"description":"Samsung's own YouTube with ads blocked, Shorts hidden and sponsors skipped (TizenTube). Local proxy; fetches one pinned script from cdn.jsdelivr.net.","author":"andrearicci93","permissions":["exec"],"ui":{"label":"Ad-free YouTube"},"intercepts":[{"appId":"com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt","label":"YouTube"}]},"files":{"README.md":"# Ad-free YouTube\n\nSamsung's own YouTube app on your TV, **without ads**. The plugin opens the YouTube app that is already on the TV and adds\na script to its page: ads blocked, Shorts hidden, sponsor segments skipped ([SponsorBlock](https://sponsor.ajay.app)),\noptional [DeArrow](https://dearrow.ajay.app) titles. You stay signed in, voice search and the TV's player keep working, and\n**nothing is installed on the TV**: no WGT, no Developer mode, no re-signing, no second YouTube app.\n\n## What you get\n\n- Ads blocked before and inside videos, as far as the script keeps up with YouTube (see *Limits*).\n- Shorts removed from the menu, SponsorBlock skipping, optional DeArrow titles and thumbnails.\n- Your own account, history and subscriptions: it is the real YouTube app, not a clone.\n- The YouTube tile of the **Vetro launcher** opens the patched app while this Shard is on. The Shard says so in its manifest\n  (`intercepts`), and the dashboard shows **Intercepts the YouTube app** on its card and in the install question.\n- An optional switch so Samsung's own YouTube button (Home tile, remote key, voice) opens the patched app.\n- If anything fails (proxy down, script missing, certificate missing) YouTube still opens, just without the patches.\n\n## Install and use\n\n1. In the dashboard open **Vetro Shards → Load plugin catalog**, find **Ad-free YouTube** and install it. It lands switched off.\n2. Switch it on, open its tab, press **Open YouTube**. The first start takes up to a minute: it makes a certificate, copies the\n   YouTube app's content folder (about 3 MB) and downloads the script once.\n3. Optional: switch on **Samsung's YouTube button opens this** (see *The Home tile*).\n\n**Remove it cleanly:** switch the tile option off, press **Remove certificate and files**, switch the plugin off, then remove\nit. Removing the plugin alone leaves the certificate and the copy of the content folder on the TV.\n\n**Tested on:** a Samsung Q80A (firmware 2310.0, Tizen 6.0) rooted with Vetro. Other models should work if they have the Cobalt\nYouTube app (`com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`); the plugin says \"Samsung YouTube not found\" when they do not. On Tizen 9 the proxy uses the TV's\nnetwork address (*Where the proxy listens*): written from a report on a 2025 Frame, not yet confirmed on a Tizen 9 TV. Not yet confirmed:\nthe real remote YouTube key after a cold boot, and long-term behaviour as YouTube changes.\n\n## How it works\n\nThe YouTube app on the TV is Cobalt (`com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`). It accepts a proxy and a content folder on its command line.\nThe plugin starts it with both:\n\n```\napp_launcher -s com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt -u 5001 USERDATA ' --base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv --dial_name=YouTube --use_eden --start_frag=#start --proxy=127.0.0.2:8101,direct:// --content=/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt'\n```\n\n- **The first four flags** are the ones Samsung's own YouTube tile passes. The proxy list ends in `direct://`: if the proxy is\n  down, the app connects directly (unpatched) instead of failing.\n- **The proxy** runs inside Vetro (where: see *Where the proxy listens*). Every host is a plain tunnel except `www.youtube.com`, whose start page\n  gets `/vetro-youtube/prelude.js` (to sanitize `fetch`/`XHR`/`JSON.parse` ad payloads on Tizen 9) and `/vetro-youtube/userscript.js`. If the certificate or the script is missing, the proxy only tunnels: YouTube then runs unpatched\n  instead of breaking.\n- **The app's own requests to the TV.** While it runs, the app sends plain requests to `http://localhost:8080` (the TV's web\n  server), for example to tell the TV which cast session it is. Through the proxy these would fail, and the phone would then\n  list the TV twice while the app is open (one entry that does nothing). So the proxy passes on those requests, and only\n  those: plain HTTP to `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` on port 8080, nothing else.\n- **The certificate.** The plugin makes a certificate authority of its own and adds it to a *copy* of the YouTube app's content\n  folder (`/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt`, a short path on purpose: see *The Home tile*). Only the YouTube app started by this plugin trusts it. The TV's trust store is never touched, and\n  `ca.key` is readable by root only, and `<DIR>` itself belongs to root: the only folder the apps' user can write in is\n  `<DIR>/cache` (the downloaded script, checked by hash on every read), so it cannot swap a file for a link that a root command follows.\n- **The script** is [TizenTube](https://github.com/reisxd/TizenTube) (reisxd, GPL-3.0), one exact release, downloaded from\n  npm's CDN on first use and used only if its SHA-256 matches the one in the plugin. It is not part of this plugin. Sponsor\n  segments come from the public [SponsorBlock](https://sponsor.ajay.app) database (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).\n\n`<DIR>` is `/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-youtube`.\n\n## Where the proxy listens\n\n- **Tizen 8 and older: `127.0.0.2`**, on the TV itself, as before. Nothing else on the network can reach it.\n- **Tizen 9 and newer: the TV's own network address** (`192.168.x.y:8101`). Some firmware does not let apps connect to `127.x` at all (a 2025 Frame\n  showed it): the YouTube app then never reaches the proxy and, because the proxy list ends in `direct://`, quietly connects straight to YouTube, so\n  it opens normally, with ads, and the plugin shows `tunnels: 0`. On the network address it works. The proxy then listens on all addresses\n  but **drops every connection that does not come from the TV itself** (loopback or one of the TV's own addresses), so another device on your network\n  cannot use it as a proxy, and nothing but this plugin's own YouTube app talks to it.\n- To choose by hand put `{\"proxy\": \"loopback\"}` or `{\"proxy\": \"lan\"}` in the plugin's `config.json` (default: automatic) and switch the plugin off and on.\n- `/api/status` shows `proxyMode`, the address and `accepted` (connections the app made to the proxy). **`accepted: 0` after opening YouTube\n  means the app never reached the proxy.** The log says when the first connection came and from where.\n- **Samsung's YouTube button and a long address.** Samsung's start settings take at most 127 characters, and the flags with `192.168.1.123` fill 123. A\n  longer address (`192.168.100.123`) does not fit: the card then says so. The Vetro launcher tile and **Open YouTube** have no such limit.\n\n## The Vetro launcher tile\n\nWith Vetro UI → Launcher on, the launcher's YouTube tile starts this Shard instead of the app: Vetro asks the Shard's `launch()`, which does what\n**Open YouTube** does (certificate, script and the proxy flags below) and starts `com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt` as the app's own user. The first press after\ninstalling can take up to a minute while the certificate and the content folder are made. Nothing else of the launcher changes.\n\n- It needs no switch of its own: **the Shard being on is the switch.** Switch the Shard off and the tile starts YouTube as before.\n- If the Shard cannot start it (proxy down, script missing, anything it throws, or no answer within 2 minutes) **Vetro starts YouTube the normal way**, unpatched,\n  so the tile never goes dead. The launcher's status says why in `lastShardLaunch`.\n- It does not depend on Samsung's wrapper app (`9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube`): the tile uses the Cobalt app directly, so it keeps working on a TV where the wrapper has been removed.\n- Commands: the same `app_launcher -t` / `app_launcher -s` as **Open YouTube**, see *Commands it runs*.\n\n## After a boot\n\nSamsung removes the wrapper app behind the YouTube key from the TV's app list at every boot, so the tile row cannot be patched\nuntil Samsung brings it back. While **Samsung's YouTube button opens this** is on, the plugin therefore watches whether YouTube was\nstarted without its proxy flags and, if so, closes it and starts it again through the proxy (at most 3 times in 2 minutes).\nAt boot it also retries the first jobs every 3 seconds until Vetro's root agent has connected. Nothing is installed.\n\nThe watch costs almost no root commands while nothing happens:\n\n- Every 3 seconds it lists the TV's processes from inside Vetro, without root. A new process it can read is looked at directly:\n  the YouTube app's command line says whether it carries the plugin's flags.\n- A new process it cannot read (on Tizen an app usually cannot read another app's processes) that is still there 3 seconds later\n  leads to one root check (`pgrep` on the YouTube app's command line), at most one every 6 seconds. Each process is tried once.\n- One root check a minute runs anyway, in case YouTube started in a way the list did not show. None runs while the patched app is\n  open, one right after it closes. A check that fails (at boot, before Vetro's root agent is there) is tried again after 6 seconds.\n- If the process list cannot be read at all, it falls back to a root check every 6 seconds.\n- `/api/status` → `watch` shows which way it runs (`processes` or `root`), how many root checks it made, and what found the app.\n\n## The Home tile (optional, off by default)\n\nSamsung's tile, remote key and voice all start the wrapper app `9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube`, which reads its flags from one row of\nthe web app service's database (`/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db`, table `widgetinfo`, column `reserved_string_6`). The same text also\nsits in the app's `config.xml` and in the package database, but neither is read when the app starts (checked on a Q80A). The switch\nappends `--proxy=127.0.0.2:<port>,direct:// --content=/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt` to that row with the `sqlite3` command, and\ntakes it out again. The rules:\n\n- **The TV passes the app at most 127 characters of that value** (it cuts the rest silently, so the app would start without\n  `--content`, not trust the plugin's certificate, and show a white screen). Samsung's value is 88 characters, so the plugin\n  takes out `--base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv` (the address the app uses anyway when it is not given) and puts it back in front\n  when it restores. That is why the content folder has a short path, and why a value that would not fit is left alone.\n- The row is patched only while the proxy is listening and the certificate and script are ready; otherwise (and when the switch\n  goes off, when the plugin is switched off, when Vetro stops, and on *Remove certificate and files*) it is put back.\n  All changes to the row go through one queue, so a slow patch can never land after a restore. A failed restore is retried.\n- Each write only happens if the row still holds what was read (compare-and-swap); only that row of that one app is touched;\n  values with quotes, `$`, backticks or non-ASCII text are never written.\n- Our two flags are removed wherever they sit in the value, so a firmware that adds its own flag after them does not strand them.\n  If our flags are in a value this plugin will not edit, *Remove certificate and files* refuses and deletes nothing.\n- If Vetro dies without restoring the row, YouTube still opens (the proxy list ends in `direct://`), unpatched.\n\n## Commands it runs, all as root\n\n- Every root command is passed via `base64 -d | sh`; `launch` and `check` also use `base64`, `grep`, `awk`, `tr`, and `stat` to inspect `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` tokens and process start times on Tizen 6 and 9, and `usleep` (200 ms poll) while waiting for an existing YouTube instance to exit.\n- Open: `openssl` (make or renew the authority and the youtube.com certificate), `cp -R` of the YouTube app's content folder\n  (about 3 MB), `app_launcher -t` (and `-k` if it does not exit) and `app_launcher -s` for `com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`.\n- Close: `app_launcher -t com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`.\n- The Home tile switch: `sqlite3` on that database (read the one row, compare-and-swap update), then `chown` of the database back to its owner.\n- Remove certificate and files: puts the row back, closes YouTube and runs `rm -rf <DIR>`.\n- With **Samsung's YouTube button opens this** on, also without a button: the watch's `pgrep` and `vconftool` check (see *After a boot*) and,\n  once a minute, a read of the row.\n\nSwitching the plugin off stops the proxy but does not close a YouTube that is already open: connections already made keep\nworking and new ones fall back to a direct connection.\nRemoving the plugin does **not** remove `<DIR>`: press *Remove certificate and files* first.\n\n## Limits\n\n- Every request to youtube.com goes through a new TLS connection, so the TV does a bit more work than with the plain app.\n- A new TizenTube release needs a new version of this plugin (the hash is pinned on purpose).\n- Ads inside videos depend on the script keeping up with YouTube; if they come back, the script needs updating, not the plugin.\n- Unofficial, and YouTube's terms do not allow ad blocking. Use it on your own TV, at your own risk.\n- Port 8101 can be changed with `{\"port\": 8123}` in the plugin's `config.json`.\n- If the TV's address changes (a new lease from the router), the next start and the check every minute use the new one.\n\n## Privacy: what it connects to\n\n- `cdn.jsdelivr.net` once, to download the TizenTube script (checked by SHA-256 before use). Nothing is sent but the request.\n- `www.youtube.com`: the proxy forwards the app's own requests; it reads the start page to add the script tag and keeps nothing.\n- The script, running inside YouTube's page, talks to YouTube and to the SponsorBlock / DeArrow servers (sponsor.ajay.app,\n  dearrow.ajay.app) the way TizenTube does. This plugin collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere else.\n\n## Credits\n\nThis plugin is only the glue. The hard parts are other people's work:\n\n- **[TizenTube](https://github.com/reisxd/TizenTube)** by **reisxd** (GPL-3.0): the script that blocks the ads, and the discovery\n  that Cobalt accepts `--proxy` and `--content`, which this whole approach is built on. The script is downloaded from its npm\n  package (`@foxreis/tizentube`) and is not part of this plugin.\n- **[SponsorBlock](https://github.com/ajayyy/SponsorBlock)** and **[DeArrow](https://github.com/ajayyy/DeArrow)** by **Ajay\n  Ramachandran** and contributors: the community database of sponsor segments (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) and of titles and thumbnails.\n- **Cobalt**, Google's open-source YouTube client that Samsung ships as the TV's YouTube app.\n- **[Vetro](https://github.com/andrearicci93/vetro)** for the plugin host, and Samsung's `sqlite3`, `openssl` and\n  `app_launcher` for the rest.\n\n## Legal\n\nUnofficial and not affiliated with Google, YouTube, Samsung, TizenTube or SponsorBlock. YouTube's terms of service do not\nallow ad blocking; use it on your own TV, at your own risk. This plugin is MIT-licensed like the rest of this catalog; the\nTizenTube script it downloads keeps its own GPL-3.0 licence.\n","address.js":"'use strict';\n// Which address the YouTube app reaches the proxy on, and who may talk to it. Plain ES5, no TV commands.\n//\n// On some firmware (a 2025 Frame on Tizen 9 measured it) apps cannot connect to 127.x at all, so the YouTube app never reaches a\n// proxy on 127.0.0.2 and, because the proxy list ends in direct://, silently connects straight to YouTube: ads stay.\n// There the proxy has to be on the TV's own network address. That address is open to the LAN unless it is checked, so the\n// proxy only accepts connections that come from the TV itself (see isLocal).\n\n// \"::ffff:192.168.1.5\" is the same peer as \"192.168.1.5\".\nfunction normalize(addr) {\n    var a = String(addr || '').toLowerCase().replace(/%.*$/, '');\n    var m = /^::ffff:(\\d{1,3}(?:\\.\\d{1,3}){3})$/.exec(a);\n    return m ? m[1] : a;\n}\n\n// ifaces: the shape of os.networkInterfaces(). Every address the TV itself has, normalised.\nfunction ownAddresses(ifaces) {\n    var list = [];\n    Object.keys(ifaces || {}).forEach(function (name) {\n        (ifaces[name] || []).forEach(function (a) { if (a && a.address) list.push(normalize(a.address)); });\n    });\n    return list;\n}\n\n// True when the peer is the TV talking to itself: loopback, or one of its own addresses. Anything else (another device on the\n// network) is not allowed to use the proxy.\nfunction isLocal(remote, ifaces) {\n    var a = normalize(remote);\n    if (!a) return false;\n    if (/^127\\.\\d{1,3}\\.\\d{1,3}\\.\\d{1,3}$/.test(a) || a === '::1') return true;\n    return ownAddresses(ifaces).indexOf(a) >= 0;\n}\n\n// The TV's own IPv4 address on the network (not loopback, not link-local), or null. The first one found: a TV has one.\nfunction lanAddress(ifaces) {\n    var found = null;\n    Object.keys(ifaces || {}).forEach(function (name) {\n        (ifaces[name] || []).forEach(function (a) {\n            if (found || !a || a.internal || (a.family !== 'IPv4' && a.family !== 4)) return;\n            if (!/^\\d{1,3}(?:\\.\\d{1,3}){3}$/.test(a.address) || /^(127|169\\.254)\\./.test(a.address)) return;\n            found = a.address;\n        });\n    });\n    return found;\n}\n\n// The Tizen major version out of /etc/tizen-release (\"Tizen6/TV 6.0.0\" on a Q80A), or 0 when it cannot be told.\nfunction tizenMajor(text) {\n    var m = /(\\d+)\\.\\d+/.exec(String(text || ''));\n    return m ? parseInt(m[1], 10) : 0;\n}\n\n// 'loopback' (127.0.0.2, the default everywhere it works) or 'lan' (the TV's own address).\n// setting: the plugin's config.json \"proxy\": \"loopback\" | \"lan\" | anything else means automatic = 'lan' from Tizen 9 on.\nfunction chooseMode(setting, tizen) {\n    if (setting === 'loopback' || setting === 'lan') return setting;\n    return tizen >= 9 ? 'lan' : 'loopback';\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { normalize: normalize, ownAddresses: ownAddresses, isLocal: isLocal, lanAddress: lanAddress, tizenMajor: tizenMajor, chooseMode: chooseMode };\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Ad-free YouTube: opens Samsung's own YouTube app with a script added to its page (ad blocking, Shorts, SponsorBlock, DeArrow).\n// Nothing is installed on the TV: the app is started with a proxy and a trust store of its own, both owned by this plugin.\n// See README.md for what runs, what is written, and how to undo it. Plain ES5.\n//\n// Two ways in: the Open button, and (when switched on) Samsung's own YouTube button, by adding the same flags to the row\n// that tile reads (tile.js). The row is only ever patched while everything it needs is up, and is put back when anything is\n// not, when the plugin is switched off, and when Vetro stops. If Vetro dies without a chance to do that, the proxy list ends\n// in direct:// so YouTube still opens.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar proxyLib = require('./proxy.js');\nvar setup = require('./setup.js');\nvar tile = require('./tile.js');\nvar scriptLib = require('./userscript.js');\nvar os = require('os');\nvar address = require('./address.js');\nvar watchLib = require('./watch.js');\n\nvar PROXY_HOST = '127.0.0.2', DEFAULT_PORT = 8101;\nvar TICK_MS = 60 * 1000, SETUP_EVERY_MS = 24 * 3600 * 1000, SCRIPT_RETRY_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;\n\nvar PAGE = '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">' +\n    '<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">' +\n    '<style>body{font:15px system-ui;margin:16px;max-width:42rem}h2{margin:0 0 4px}.row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:14px 0}' +\n    'button{font:inherit;padding:8px 14px}table{border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0;width:100%}td{padding:4px 8px 4px 0;vertical-align:top}' +\n    'td:first-child{opacity:.7;white-space:nowrap}#msg{min-height:1.4em;margin:8px 0}.err{color:#c0392b}small{opacity:.75;display:block;margin-top:14px;line-height:1.45}' +\n    'label.sw{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:14px 0 4px}label.sw input{margin-top:3px;width:18px;height:18px}#tilenote{opacity:.75;margin:0 0 8px 28px;min-height:1.2em}</style>' +\n    '<body><h2>Ad-free YouTube</h2><div>Samsung’s own YouTube app, with ads, Shorts and sponsor segments handled.</div>' +\n    '<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"open\">Open YouTube</button><button id=\"close\">Close YouTube</button></div><div id=\"msg\"></div>' +\n    '<label class=\"sw\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"tile\"><span><b>Samsung’s YouTube button opens this</b><br>The Home tile, the remote’s YouTube key and voice start the patched app. ' +\n    'If Vetro is not running, YouTube still opens, just without the patches.</span></label><div id=\"tilenote\"></div>' +\n    '<table><tr><td>Certificate</td><td id=\"s_setup\">…</td></tr><tr><td>Script</td><td id=\"s_script\">…</td></tr>' +\n    '<tr><td>Proxy</td><td id=\"s_proxy\">…</td></tr><tr><td>Pages patched</td><td id=\"s_pages\">…</td></tr></table>' +\n    '<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"clean\">Remove certificate and files</button></div>' +\n    '<small>The first start makes a certificate that only this YouTube app trusts (the TV does not) and downloads the script once, ' +\n    'checked against a fixed SHA-256. The script is <b>TizenTube</b> by reisxd (GPL-3.0); sponsor segments come from the ' +\n    '<b>SponsorBlock</b> database (sponsor.ajay.app, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). Unofficial: YouTube’s terms do not allow ad blocking.</small>' +\n    '<script>' +\n    'function $(i){return document.getElementById(i)}' +\n    'function say(t,bad){var m=$(\"msg\");m.textContent=t;m.className=bad?\"err\":\"\"}' +\n    'function post(p,b){return fetch(p,{method:\"POST\",headers:{\"Content-Type\":\"text/plain\"},body:JSON.stringify(b||{})}).then(function(r){return r.json()})}' +\n    'var busy=false,pollBusy=false,pollSeq=0,cleanArmed=false,cleanReset=0;' +\n    'function resetClean(){cleanArmed=false;clearTimeout(cleanReset);$(\"clean\").textContent=\"Remove certificate and files\";}' +\n    'function show(d){$(\"s_setup\").textContent=d.setup===\"ready\"?\"ready\":d.setup===\"working\"?\"setting up…\":d.setup===\"nocobalt\"?\"Samsung YouTube not found\":d.setup===\"error\"?\"error: \"+d.error:\"not made yet\";' +\n    '$(\"s_script\").textContent=d.script===\"ready\"?\"TizenTube \"+d.scriptVersion:d.script===\"error\"?\"error: \"+d.scriptError:\"not downloaded yet\";' +\n    '$(\"s_proxy\").textContent=d.proxy===\"up\"?\"listening on \"+d.proxyAddress:d.proxyError?\"error: \"+d.proxyError:\"stopped\";' +\n    '$(\"s_pages\").textContent=d.pages?d.pages+(d.lastPage?\" (last \"+d.lastPage+\")\":\"\"):\"none yet\";' +\n    'if(!busy){$(\"tile\").checked=!!d.tileOn}' +\n    '$(\"tilenote\").textContent=d.tileState===\"on\"?\"On.\":d.tileState===\"waiting\"?\"Waiting: \"+d.tileNote:d.tileState===\"unsupported\"||d.tileState===\"error\"?d.tileNote:\"\"}' +\n    'function poll(force){if(pollBusy&&!force)return;pollBusy=true;var seq=++pollSeq;fetch(\"status\").then(function(r){return r.json()}).then(function(d){if(seq===pollSeq){pollBusy=false;show(d)}},function(){if(seq===pollSeq)pollBusy=false})}' +\n    'function fail(e){say(e&&e.message||\"Request failed\",true)}' +\n    '$(\"open\").onclick=function(){say(\"Preparing and starting… the first time takes up to a minute.\");post(\"open\").then(function(d){say(d.ok?(d.warning||\"YouTube is starting on the TV.\"):d.error,!d.ok||!!d.warning);poll(true)}).catch(fail)};' +\n    '$(\"close\").onclick=function(){post(\"close\").then(function(d){say(d&&d.ok===false?(d.error||\"Failed to close.\"):\"YouTube closed.\",d&&d.ok===false);poll(true)}).catch(fail)};' +\n    '$(\"tile\").onchange=function(){busy=true;var on=$(\"tile\").checked;say(on?\"Preparing…\":\"Switching off…\");post(\"tile\",{on:on}).then(function(d){busy=false;say(d.ok?\"\":d.error,!d.ok);poll(true)},function(e){busy=false;fail(e)})};' +\n    '$(\"clean\").onclick=function(){if(!cleanArmed){cleanArmed=true;$(\"clean\").textContent=\"Click again to remove files\";clearTimeout(cleanReset);cleanReset=setTimeout(resetClean,5000);return;}resetClean();post(\"cleanup\").then(function(d){say(d.ok?\"Removed.\":d.error,!d.ok);poll(true)}).catch(fail)};' +\n    'document.addEventListener(\"visibilitychange\",function(){if(!document.hidden)poll(true)});' +\n    'poll();setInterval(function(){if(!document.hidden)poll()},3000);' +\n    '</script></body>';\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var cfg = ctx.config.get();\n    var PORT = typeof cfg.port === 'number' && cfg.port % 1 === 0 && cfg.port >= 1024 && cfg.port < 65536 ? cfg.port : DEFAULT_PORT;\n    var script = new scriptLib.UserScript(setup.CACHE);\n    // Where the YouTube app reaches the proxy. 'loopback': 127.0.0.2, as it always was. 'lan': the TV's own network address, for\n    // firmware where apps cannot connect to 127.x (then the app silently falls back to a direct connection and the ads stay).\n    // The proxy then listens on every address and takes connections from the TV itself only (see address.js). Fixed when the plugin starts.\n    var MODE = address.chooseMode(cfg.proxy, address.tizenMajor(readText('/etc/tizen-release')));\n    var BIND = MODE === 'lan' ? '0.0.0.0' : PROXY_HOST;\n    // The address put in the app's flags: the TV's own when it has one (it can change with the router), else loopback.\n    function proxyHost() { return MODE === 'lan' ? (address.lanAddress(os.networkInterfaces()) || PROXY_HOST) : PROXY_HOST; }\n    var logLines = [], preparing = null, settingUp = null, opening = null, alive = false, timer = null, watchTimer = null;\n    var tileOn = cfg.tile === true;\n    var lastSetup = 0, nextScriptTry = 0, lastPageUnix = 0;\n    var leafCache = null, leafStamp = null;\n    var st = { setup: 'idle', error: null, script: 'idle', scriptError: null, proxyError: null, pages: 0, lastPage: null, tileState: 'off', tileNote: '' };\n\n    function log(m) { logLines.push(new Date().toISOString().slice(11, 19) + ' ' + m); if (logLines.length > 150) logLines.shift(); }\n    function exec(shell, ms) { return ctx.execute(setup.wrap(shell), ms); }\n    function noop() {}\n\n    function saveConfig(patch) {\n        var c = ctx.config.get();\n        Object.keys(patch).forEach(function (k) { c[k] = patch[k]; });\n        try { ctx.config.set(c); } catch (e) { log('config not saved: ' + e.message); }\n    }\n\n    function readText(file) { try { return fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8'); } catch (e) { return ''; } }\n\n    function readLeaf() {\n        var keyFile = path.join(setup.DIR, 'leaf.key');\n        var crtFile = path.join(setup.DIR, 'leaf.crt');\n        var caFile = path.join(setup.DIR, 'ca.crt');\n        try {\n            var ks = fs.statSync(keyFile), cs = fs.statSync(crtFile), as = fs.statSync(caFile);\n            var stamp = ks.mtime.getTime() + ':' + ks.size + '|' + cs.mtime.getTime() + ':' + cs.size + '|' + as.mtime.getTime() + ':' + as.size;\n            if (leafCache && leafStamp === stamp) return leafCache;\n            var key = fs.readFileSync(keyFile);\n            var cert = fs.readFileSync(crtFile, 'utf8') + fs.readFileSync(caFile, 'utf8');\n            leafCache = { key: key, cert: cert };\n            leafStamp = stamp;\n            return leafCache;\n        } catch (e) {\n            if (preparing && leafCache) return leafCache;\n            if (settingUp && leafCache) return leafCache;\n            leafCache = null;\n            leafStamp = null;\n            return null;\n        }\n    }\n    function contentThere() { try { return fs.statSync(path.join(setup.CONTENT, 'ssl', 'certs')).isDirectory(); } catch (e) { return false; } }\n\n    var proxy = proxyLib.createProxy({\n        host: BIND, port: PORT, log: log,\n        allow: MODE === 'lan' ? function (remote) { return address.isLocal(remote, os.networkInterfaces()); } : null,\n        leaf: readLeaf,\n        script: function () { return script.load(); },\n        onPage: function () { st.pages++; lastPageUnix = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000); st.lastPage = new Date().toISOString().slice(11, 19); }\n    });\n\n    function listen() {\n        return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n            proxy.listen(function (e) {\n                if (e) { st.proxyError = e.code === 'EADDRINUSE' ? 'port ' + PORT + ' is in use (put {\"port\": 8123} in config.json to change it)' : e.message; reject(new Error(st.proxyError)); }\n                else { st.proxyError = null; resolve(); }\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function runSetup() {\n        if (settingUp) return settingUp;\n        st.setup = 'working'; st.error = null;\n        settingUp = exec(setup.setupScript(), 90000).then(function (r) {\n            settingUp = null;\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (/^nocobalt$/m.test(out)) { st.setup = 'nocobalt'; throw new Error('Samsung’s YouTube app was not found on this TV'); }\n            if (!/^ready$/m.test(out)) { st.setup = 'error'; st.error = String((r && r.stderr) || out || 'setup failed').slice(0, 200); throw new Error(st.error); }\n            st.setup = 'ready'; lastSetup = Date.now();\n        }, function (e) {\n            settingUp = null;\n            if (st.setup === 'working') { st.setup = 'error'; st.error = e.message; }\n            throw e;\n        });\n        return settingUp;\n    }\n\n    function runScript() {\n        return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n            script.ensure(function (e) {\n                if (e) { st.script = 'error'; st.scriptError = e.message; nextScriptTry = Date.now() + SCRIPT_RETRY_MS; reject(e); }\n                else { st.script = 'ready'; st.scriptError = null; resolve(); }\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Certificate, script, proxy, in that order. The script is not essential: without it the proxy only tunnels and YouTube\n    // runs unpatched, so its failure is reported as a warning. Concurrent callers share one run.\n    // Resolves to {warning}; rejects when there is no certificate setup or no proxy.\n    function prepare() {\n        if (preparing) return preparing;\n        log('preparing');\n        var warning = null;\n        preparing = runSetup().then(function () { return runScript().catch(function (e) { warning = 'The script could not be downloaded (' + e.message + '): YouTube opens without the patches.'; }); })\n            .then(function () { return proxy.listening() ? null : listen(); })\n            .then(function () { preparing = null; log(warning ? 'ready, without the script' : 'ready'); return { warning: warning }; },\n                function (e) { preparing = null; log('prepare failed: ' + e.message); throw e; });\n        return preparing;\n    }\n\n    // Why the row may not be patched right now ('' when it may).\n    function blocker() {\n        if (!tileOn) return 'switched off';\n        if (!proxy.listening()) return st.proxyError ? st.proxyError : 'the proxy is not running';\n        if (!readLeaf() || !contentThere()) return 'the certificate is not ready';\n        if (!script.load()) return 'the script is not downloaded yet';\n        return '';\n    }\n\n    // Everything that changes the row goes through this queue, one job at a time, so a slow patch can never land after a restore.\n    var queue = Promise.resolve();\n    function serial(fn) { var r = queue.then(fn, fn); queue = r.then(noop, noop); return r; }\n\n    // Makes the row match what is wanted: patched when tile is on and everything is up, original otherwise. Idempotent.\n    // The decision is taken when the job runs, not when it is asked for; calls made while one is waiting share it.\n    var waiting = null, restoreTries = 0, retryTimer = null, bootTries = 0;\n    // The plugin starts before Vetro's root agent has connected (every boot), so the first jobs fail with \"no root agent\n    // connected\". Try again every few seconds instead of waiting for the next minute tick.\n    function retrySoon() {\n        if (!alive || !tileOn || retryTimer || bootTries++ >= 60) return;\n        retryTimer = setTimeout(function () {\n            retryTimer = null;\n            if (!alive || !tileOn) return;\n            var chain = !(readLeaf() && script.load() && contentThere())\n                ? prepare().catch(function (e) { log('retry: ' + e.message); retrySoon(); })\n                : (!proxy.listening() ? listen().catch(function (e) { log('proxy: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve());\n            chain.then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('retry: ' + e.message); });\n        }, 3000);\n        if (retryTimer && retryTimer.unref) retryTimer.unref();\n    }\n    function reconcile() {\n        if (waiting) return waiting;\n        waiting = serial(function () {\n            waiting = null;\n            var why = alive ? blocker() : 'the plugin is off';\n            var job = why ? tile.restore(exec) : tile.apply(exec, proxyHost(), PORT);\n            return job.then(function (state) {\n                if (why) {\n                    st.tileState = tileOn && alive ? 'waiting' : 'off'; st.tileNote = tileOn ? why : '';\n                    if (state === 'error' || state === 'raced' || state === 'patched' || state === 'stuck') {\n                        log('row restore: ' + state);\n                        // The flags are still there. Try again soon, a few times; the direct:// fallback keeps YouTube opening meanwhile.\n                        if (alive && restoreTries++ < 5 && !retryTimer) {\n                            retryTimer = setTimeout(function () { retryTimer = null; if (alive) reconcile(); }, 5000);\n                            if (retryTimer && retryTimer.unref) retryTimer.unref();\n                        }\n                    } else restoreTries = 0;\n                    return state;\n                }\n                restoreTries = 0;\n                if (state === 'patched') { if (st.tileState !== 'on') log('Samsung’s YouTube button now opens the patched app'); st.tileState = 'on'; st.tileNote = ''; }\n                else if (state === 'absent') { st.tileState = 'unsupported'; st.tileNote = 'This TV has no entry for Samsung’s YouTube app that can be changed.'; }\n                else if (state === 'toolong') { st.tileState = 'unsupported'; st.tileNote = 'The TV’s address (' + proxyHost() + ') is too long to fit in Samsung’s YouTube settings. Use the Vetro launcher’s YouTube tile, or the Open button.'; }\n                else if (state === 'foreign') { st.tileState = 'unsupported'; st.tileNote = 'Samsung’s YouTube settings are not in the expected form: left as they are.'; }\n                else { st.tileState = 'error'; st.tileNote = 'The TV’s app list could not be updated (' + state + '); trying again.'; log('row: ' + state); retrySoon(); }\n                if (st.tileState === 'on') bootTries = 0;\n                return state;\n            }, function (e) { st.tileState = 'error'; st.tileNote = 'Could not reach the TV’s app list: ' + e.message; log('row: ' + e.message); if (!why) retrySoon(); return 'error'; });\n        });\n        return waiting;\n    }\n\n    // Once a minute while the button is on: keeps the proxy up, renews what expires, retries a failed download, and puts the row\n    // right again if Samsung rewrote it (an app update does).\n    function tick() {\n        if (!alive || !tileOn || preparing || settingUp) return;\n        bootTries = 0;\n        var chain = Promise.resolve();\n        if (Date.now() - lastSetup > SETUP_EVERY_MS) chain = chain.then(function () { return runSetup().catch(function (e) { log('setup: ' + e.message); }); });\n        if (!script.load() && Date.now() > nextScriptTry && contentThere()) chain = chain.then(function () { return runScript().catch(noop); });\n        chain.then(function () { if (!proxy.listening() && readLeaf() && script.load() && contentThere()) return listen().catch(function (e) { log('proxy: ' + e.message); }); })\n            .then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('tick: ' + e.message); });\n    }\n\n    // Samsung's YouTube started by the remote key, the Home tile or voice, without our flags (the TV's entry for it is missing after\n    // a boot, or Samsung rewrote it): close it and start it again through the proxy. At most 3 times in 2 minutes.\n    // The root check (setup.checkScript) only runs when the process list shows something new that Vetro cannot read itself\n    // (watch.js), once a minute as a backstop, or every CHECK_MS when the process list cannot be read at all.\n    var watcher = new watchLib.Watcher(), watchBusy = false, relaunches = [], lastWhy = '', lastOut = null;\n    var wst = { checks: 0, seen: 0, backstop: 0 };\n    function relaunch(how) {\n        relaunches.push(Date.now());\n        log('YouTube was started without the patches (' + how + '): starting it again through the proxy');\n        return exec(setup.launchScript(proxyHost(), PORT, { forceRestart: true }), 25000);\n    }\n    function watch() {\n        if (!alive || !tileOn || watchBusy) return;\n        var why = blocker();\n        if (why) { if (why !== lastWhy) log('watch idle: ' + why); lastWhy = why; watcher.blocked(); return; }\n        lastWhy = '';\n        var now = Date.now();\n        relaunches = relaunches.filter(function (t) { return now - t < 120000; });\n        // live > 0: the patched app is open, and there is only one.\n        var a = watcher.step(now, proxy.stats().live > 0, relaunches.length < 3);\n        if (a.blind) log('watch: cannot list processes (' + a.blind + '): checking as root every ' + (watchLib.CHECK_MS / 1000) + ' s');\n        if (a.relaunch) {\n            wst.seen++; watchBusy = true;\n            relaunch('seen in the process list').then(function () { watchBusy = false; }, function (e) { watchBusy = false; log('watch: ' + e.message); });\n            return;\n        }\n        if (!a.check) return;\n        var backstop = a.check === 'backstop';\n        watchBusy = true; wst.checks++;\n        exec(setup.checkScript(), 10000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (!/^relaunch$/m.test(out)) { if (out !== lastOut) log('watch: ' + (out.trim() || 'YouTube not running')); lastOut = out; return null; }\n            if (backstop) wst.backstop++;\n            return relaunch(backstop ? 'found by the once-a-minute check' : 'found by the root check');\n        }).then(function () { watchBusy = false; }, function (e) { watchBusy = false; watcher.failed(); log('watch: ' + e.message); });\n    }\n\n    function json(res, code, body) { res.writeHead(code, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); }\n\n    function readJson(req, cb) {\n        var data = '', done = false;\n        function end(v) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(v); } }\n        req.on('data', function (c) { data += c; if (data.length > 2048) { req.destroy(); end({}); } });\n        req.on('end', function () { var v; try { v = JSON.parse(data || '{}'); } catch (e) { v = {}; } end(v && typeof v === 'object' ? v : {}); });\n        req.on('error', function () { end({}); });\n    }\n\n    // Gets the certificate and script ready (the first time up to a minute) and starts YouTube through the proxy.\n    // Resolves with { warning } and rejects when YouTube did not start. Used by the Open button and by the launcher tile.\n    function openYoutube() {\n        if (opening) return opening;\n        var warning = null;\n        var p = prepare().then(function (r) { warning = r.warning; return exec(setup.launchScript(proxyHost(), PORT, { lastPageUnix: lastPageUnix }), 25000); }).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (!/successfully launched/.test(out)) throw new Error('YouTube did not start: ' + out.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 120));\n            log('YouTube started');\n            return { warning: warning };\n        }).then(function (res) {\n            if (opening === p) opening = null;\n            return res;\n        }, function (e) {\n            if (opening === p) opening = null;\n            throw e;\n        });\n        opening = p;\n        return p;\n    }\n\n    function snapshot() {\n        var have = script.load(), s = proxy.stats();\n        return { setup: st.setup, error: st.error, script: have ? 'ready' : st.script, scriptVersion: scriptLib.VERSION, scriptError: st.scriptError,\n            proxy: proxy.listening() ? 'up' : 'down', proxyAddress: proxyHost() + ':' + PORT, proxyMode: MODE, proxyError: st.proxyError, pages: st.pages, lastPage: st.lastPage,\n            tileOn: tileOn, tileState: st.tileState, tileNote: st.tileNote, tunnels: s.tunnels, opened: s.opened, live: s.live, accepted: s.accepted, refused: s.refused, foreign: s.foreign,\n            watch: { mode: watcher.blind ? 'root' : 'processes', rootChecks: wst.checks, foundInList: wst.seen, foundByBackstop: wst.backstop } };\n    }\n\n    return {\n        // manifest \"intercepts\": Vetro's launcher calls this when the YouTube tile is pressed, instead of starting the app itself.\n        // Anything but a failure to start (declining, an error) makes Vetro start YouTube the normal way, unpatched.\n        launch: function (appId) {\n            if (appId !== setup.APP) return Promise.resolve(false);\n            return openYoutube().then(function () { return true; });\n        },\n        // Starts the proxy only when certificate, script AND content folder from an earlier run are all present (preventing\n        // MITM-before-content TLS errors), and brings the row in line: patched when the button is on, original otherwise.\n        // A first run does nothing until the page asks.\n        start: function () {\n            alive = true;\n            restoreTries = 0;\n            bootTries = 0;\n            if (retryTimer) { clearTimeout(retryTimer); retryTimer = null; }\n            if (timer) clearInterval(timer);\n            timer = setInterval(function () { try { tick(); } catch (e) { log('tick: ' + e.message); } }, TICK_MS);\n            if (timer.unref) timer.unref();\n            if (watchTimer) clearInterval(watchTimer);\n            watchTimer = setInterval(function () { try { watch(); } catch (e) { log('watch: ' + e.message); } }, watchLib.SCAN_MS);\n            if (watchTimer.unref) watchTimer.unref();\n            var allReady = !!(readLeaf() && script.load() && contentThere());\n            var ready = allReady ? listen().catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve();\n            ready.then(function () { return tileOn && !allReady ? prepare().catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); retrySoon(); }) : null; })\n                .then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); });\n        },\n        // Puts the tile row back first so YouTube never sees a patched row pointing at a closed port, then stops listening.\n        stop: function () {\n            alive = false;\n            opening = null;\n            lastPageUnix = 0;\n            if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }\n            if (watchTimer) { clearInterval(watchTimer); watchTimer = null; }\n            if (retryTimer) { clearTimeout(retryTimer); retryTimer = null; }\n            // Resolves once the row is restored and the proxy closes (or timeout elapses), so a fallback timer never outlives stop().\n            return new Promise(function (resolve) {\n                var done = false, late = null;\n                var closeProxy = function () {\n                    if (done) return;\n                    done = true;\n                    if (late) clearTimeout(late);\n                    lastPageUnix = 0;\n                    if (!alive) proxy.close();\n                    resolve();\n                };\n                late = setTimeout(closeProxy, 30000);\n                if (late.unref) late.unref();\n                reconcile().then(closeProxy, closeProxy);\n            });\n        },\n        status: function () { return { running: alive, proxy: proxy.listening(), setup: st.setup, script: script.load() ? scriptLib.VERSION : null, tile: st.tileState }; },\n        onAgent: function (connected) {\n            if (!connected || !alive || !tileOn) return;\n            bootTries = 0;\n            if (retryTimer) { clearTimeout(retryTimer); retryTimer = null; }\n            watcher.failed();\n            var chain = !(readLeaf() && script.load() && contentThere())\n                ? prepare().catch(function (e) { log('agent: ' + e.message); retrySoon(); })\n                : (!proxy.listening() ? listen().catch(function (e) { log('proxy: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve());\n            chain.then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('agent: ' + e.message); });\n        },\n\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(PAGE);\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'status' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, 200, snapshot()); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'log' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, 200, { log: logLines }); return true; }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n            if (sub === 'open') {\n                openYoutube().then(function (r) {\n                    json(res, 200, r.warning ? { ok: true, warning: r.warning } : { ok: true });\n                }).catch(function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'close') {\n                lastPageUnix = 0;\n                ctx.execute(setup.closeScript(), 15000).then(function () { json(res, 200, { ok: true }); }, function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'tile') {\n                readJson(req, function (body) {\n                    if (typeof body.on !== 'boolean') { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: 'Send {\"on\": true|false}' }); return; }\n                    tileOn = body.on;\n                    saveConfig({ tile: tileOn });\n                    var go = tileOn ? prepare().then(noop, function (e) { log('tile: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve();\n                    go.then(function () { return reconcile(); }).then(function () { json(res, 200, { ok: true, state: st.tileState, note: st.tileNote }); },\n                        function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'cleanup') {\n                // The row first, in line with every other change to it: it points at files that are about to go.\n                lastPageUnix = 0;\n                tileOn = false; saveConfig({ tile: false });\n                serial(function () {\n                    return tile.restore(exec).then(function (state) {\n                        if (state !== 'original' && state !== 'absent' && state !== 'foreign') throw new Error('Samsung’s YouTube button could not be put back (' + state + '): nothing was removed');\n                        proxy.close(true); script.forget(); leafCache = null; leafStamp = null;\n                        return ctx.execute(setup.cleanupScript(), 30000);\n                    });\n                }).then(function () { st.setup = 'idle'; st.script =